This is my fourth ascension, and i must say that it was by far the
easiest game i ever had and hardest class i ever played. Since my
Priest ascension i concentrated on monks. This has proven to be a
difficult task, and i lost many many rekrutacjas before this one. One
made it to Master Kaen, but failed to defeat him - i expected him to
be no more powerful than Asmodeus and the likes, but this was not the
case. Other was drowned by some aquatic monster late in the game, with
full ascension kit.
This particular game (my monk was a neutral human) started with huge
RNG smile: on level 3 there was a huuuge hardware shop with 6 (!)
magic lamps, and on level 4 co-aligned altar. I made it quickly to
Oracle and started to convert all my unidentified potions to water. In
the process Oracle got killed, and i do not really know how. I was
zapping some wands in hope one of those is cancellation, than moved
outside Oracle shrine to fight some enemies, got back - and saw Medusa
is no more. If there was some message i missed it in the fight. None
of the wands was death.
I prayed for holy water, blessed my lamps, and decided to go for
artifacts with wishes: the blessed Eye of the Aethiopica and blessed
The Orb of Fate. That gave me magic resistance, luckstone and means of
teleporting away from troubles among other benefits. Other wishes have
been burned for boots of speed, fireproof t-shirt and magic marker for
scrolls of enchant armor and identify.
On the lest level of Sokoban i had a second smile from RNG, as i found
both bag of holding and amulet of reflection. This made me pretty much
ready for Castle. I visited Mine Town in the mean time, but found
nothing interesting there. Altar was lawful, i converted it much later
to neutral, but on this stage i simply donated for one more AC point.
With wand of polymorph i made my pets little bit more powerful, but
they kept dying anyway (even my troll quickly passed out after being
engulfed by trapper, i believe), so for the remaining of the game i
had to rely on myself.
Castle was simply. I cleared monsters with help of conflict, got my
wand of wishing and didn't bothered with dragons and other nasties
below. I was pretty much ready for quest.
My wishes from Castle wand gone for gauntlets of dexterity, helm of
brilliance, two magic markers and spellbook of sleep - i needed the
last one to win Master Kaen, and couldn't get in a lengthy session of
polypiling (i got other important books in the process however). This
wish had proven to be a smart choice, as a sleep spell was essential
to my survival - Master Kaen was probably the worst enemy i ever
fought. Even well prepared i needed to branchport to Sokoban in order
to survive. However finally he died and that was the last serious
obstacle (other potential obstacles have been genocided on this stage)
on my way to deity.
I never made it to Fort Ludios and Mines End. Fort Ludios doesn't seem
to be a place worth visiting at all, usually on this stage of the game
you probably do need money or food any more. Mines End has luckstone,
but i had it from Orb of Fate.
In the castle i couldn't resist temptation and ate black dragon
corpse, thus ruining my food conducts. After that everything was easy.
I dived deep into dungeon down to vibrating square (Demogorgon being
the only serious opponent, but i was ready to handle him), got all 3
items and in a proper order, and with conflict on for the rest of my
travel fought for Amulet. Mysterious force was merciless - i think i
visited Orcus Town 6 or 7 times, but once i left Gehennom the rest was
a piece of cake. Even on planes i felt confident. All 3 riders chased
me, but once i learned how to deal with them (magic missile rules)
they also doesn't seem to be so scary. Second altar was mine.

all the best
rekrutacja



